	(text "DESIGN VALUES (LM74910H-Q1 SNOSDE6C sec. 9.2; Node60 DEC-001). Values per DropOut D-45.\nR(ILIM) = 12 x RSET / (RSENSE x ILIM) = 12 x 49.9 / (0.25m x 32k) = 74.9 A breaker (Rev A: 75 A).\n  RSET 49.9R: E96 value nearest the 50R in Rev A (50-100R allowed). R(ILIM) 32k: E192, 1 %.\nFast SCP: ISCP to RSENSE_P through R204 0R (no RISCP shift) -> 20 mV default = 80 A.\n  R204 keeps the RISCP option (VSNS_SCP = 10.5 uA x RISCP + 20 mV); C212 is the DNP deglitch option (D-48).\nCTMR 68nF C0G: T(OC) = 1.2 x 68n / 82.3u = 0.99 ms; retry = 22.7e6 x 68n = 1.5 s. Tune vs inrush (GATE-PWR-01).\nCCAP 470nF 50V: >= 10 x sum(Ciss) of Q201-Q204; re-check when the FETs are chosen. CVS 100nF 100V.\nRG 10R + Cdvdt 10nF on HGATE: inrush slew = 55 uA / 10 nF = 5.5 V/ms.\nOV/UV/BATT_MON ladder, 118.97k total (< 120k leakage rule), 1 %:\n  OV rising = 0.60 V x 118.97k / 2.1k  = 34.0 V   (disconnects above 34 V; passes 24 V jump start)\n  UVLO fall = 0.55 V x 118.97k / 11.97k = 5.47 V  (rising 0.60 V -> 5.96 V)\n  BATT_MON = SW x 9.97k / 118.97k = SW / 11.93 (1:12 concept); 3.3 V full scale = 39.4 V\n  BATT_MON source 9.1 k with 10nF C0G (tau 91 us): set the ADC sample time from this.\n  The SW switch opens in SLEEP, so the ladder draws nothing while parked.\nEN tied to VS (always on). SLEEP = INH: parked = SLEEP mode (6 uA; OUT fed by the 7R bypass, 100 mA peak).\nSLEEP_OV = OUT: overvoltage CLAMP mode while parked (~21 V), so VDDAU stays up through a jump start.\nIMON floating (INA228 fitted). RTN pad floating per datasheet. FLT 10k pull-up to 3V3_MAIN (low when off).\nINA228 A1 = A0 = GND -> 0x40; ALERT unused. ADCRANGE = 1 (+/-40.96 mV); SHUNT_CAL in firmware.\nTMP175 A2..A0 = GND -> 0x48. Place beside the FET bank. NTC tight to the RSENSE body (GATE-TMP-01).\nNTC_RSENSE: 10k 0.1 % over NTC, ratiometric to VREFH = 3V3_MAIN; 5 k source, 100nF C0G (tau 0.5 ms).\nRSENSE Kelvin: two separate star pairs from the sense pads, one to U201 (via R203/R204), one to U202.\nCapacitors on battery nets are 100 V (>= 2x the 34 V OV cut-off, derating rule).\nMOSFETs: 2 + 2 drawn as placeholders; count and part follow the surge/thermal calculation (DEC-001).\nEMI filter on the regulator branch only; L201 and C208 TBD (finalize after emissions test).\nUNVERIFIED (release-blocking): FET count/part, RSENSE part, EMI filter values, parked leakage of U202 inputs.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
